    "bounding box" : [ 83.338, 604.18, 511.934, 650.365 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "where U(y) = 1 − y2. The perturbed flow is incompressible, ∇⃗ · ⃗u = 0, and we impose no-slip boundary conditions Φ(t,±1) = ∂yΦ(t,±1) = 0. In order to correctly account for energy in the system we work to second order in perturbation theory,"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 4,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 194.449, 560.148, 511.938, 592.605 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "δP = ϵP(1)(t,x,y) + ϵ2P(2)(t,x,y) + O(ϵ)3 (A.6) Φ = ϵΦ(1)(t,x,y) + ϵ2Φ(2)(t,x,y) + O(ϵ)3, (A.7)"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 5,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 83.338, 519.105, 511.943, 546.273 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "where ϵ is a formal parameter counting orders in the expansion. Let us consider each order in turn."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 6,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 103.662, 477.683, 511.938, 513.755 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "At O(ϵ) we take a real perturbation formed as follows: Φ(1)(t,x,y) = ϕ(t,y)eiαx + ϕ(t,y)e−iαx (A.8)"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 8,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 83.338, 420.76, 511.94, 465.942 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "with wavenumber α ̸= 0. P(1) is determined algebraically by the x-component of (A.1) at order ϵ. The y component of (A.1), after inserting P(1), gives the Orr-Sommerfeld equation (2.1), where the Orr-Sommerfeld operator is"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 9,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 182.496, 388.23, 511.938, 409.5 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "OOS = −∆−2 1 (iαRe)−1∆22 − U(y)∆2 + U′′(y) , (A.9)"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 10,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 83.338, 354.933, 511.933, 384.087 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "with Reynolds number Re = ν−1, and where ∆2 = ∂y2 − α2 is the spatial Laplacian for the x,y-plane."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 11,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 103.662, 312.988, 472.468, 351.338 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "At O(ϵ)2 we have perturbations sourced by O(ϵ) terms. These take the form, Φ(2)(t,x,y) = δϕ0(t,y) +"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
